# P1: the device profile of c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-w1 AT EIGHT USERS, copying the tp4-262k8-best-jobs P1 conventions (the tp4-profile2-jobs conventions): status, an all-four reset and two gate arms on the SAME eight real-text coding
# prompts (8 x 4,096 tokens; user 0 asks 256 tokens out, the others 128, all ignore_eos): ops-twin unprofiled (the per-round trace_ms, the [PACKED-*] and [PHASE] splits and the texts), ops-trace profiled (tracy, op-support 20000 - 200000 segfaults
# the dispatch thread, any other count is refused - the CPP post-process only, a read-back after every 2nd verify replay, no prefill flush). One container gives 8-live rounds (two 64-row blocks), then the live count falls as users finish.
# NEVER CANCEL this job once the gate step has started: the profiler writes as root and a cancel can leave root-owned files that break the next checkout. A segfault in read_core_data_from_completion_queue is INFRA: do not raise op-support.
# Disk: the profile tree up to 4 GB; the guard stops the arm at 4 GB or 85% disk. NEVER delete the P8 base image.
# READ: ops-trace texts equal ops-twin's; THE DELIVERED PER-LEVER GAINS COME FROM HERE: the per-op table of one 64-row block's verify against the tp4-262k8-best-jobs P1 (the control's): the reduce-scatter and all-gather rows (U1: about -4 ms), the sampler tail (nosamp: about
# -4.35 ms a verify), the quad draft's conv and head-copy rows (D2a and D2c: about -8.5 ms an eight-seat round), the per-live-count table, and the gap between the traces (the host-gap stage 1: about -20 ms). Duration (estimate): 150 min (100 best, 210 worst). Soft.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/w1 eight-seat 262k stack window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/w1 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a
# registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-w1-1 is what B0 builds from the pushed tp4/w1 commit; every later job serves that one image. A commit of a
# file the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=status reset gate
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-w1-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-w1
C2_GATE_PLAN=ops-twin,ops-trace
C2_GATE_JIT=record
